; ==== OPERATOR-BAHO BOSHI ====
; Post-call operator survey (call-center repo: infra/pbx/operator-survey). Managed by install.sh / rollback.sh.
; ext-queues adds VQ_CONTINUE to the Queue() options ("c": the caller stays in the dialplan when the operator
; hangs up) and goes to VQ_DEST after Queue() returns, INSTEAD of the queue's failover. These are globals, so they
; apply to every queue: install.sh refuses to install while the PBX has more than one queue.
; BAHO_FAILOVER is the failover destination of queue @BAHO_QUEUE@ (context^exten^priority) that [operator-baho]
; sends a caller to when there was no conversation. Turn the survey off: rollback.sh.
VQ_CONTINUE = c
VQ_DEST = operator-baho^s^1
BAHO_FAILOVER = @BAHO_FAILOVER@
; ==== OPERATOR-BAHO OXIRI ====
